  "term": "epidural hematoma",
  "definition": "Epidural hematoma, described here as acute epidural hematoma (AEDH), is a brain injury finding seen in people with traumatic brain injury. In this source, it is identified as a factor associated with in-hospital death and with unfavorable outcomes 6 months after injury.",
